<title>UK: Virgin Atlantic to add two new U.S. flights.</title>
<headline>Virgin Atlantic to add two new U.S. flights.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>British airline Virgin Atlantic said on Wednesday it had decided to lay on two additional flights between London and New York on Friday evening as a result of the strike at rival British Airways Plc.</p>
<p>A spokesman told Reuters that the airline was also looking at putting on other extra flights where appropriate.</p>
<p>Virgin Atlantic said that apart from the additional flights announced on Wednesday, seats on all its aircraft had been sold through to Sunday.</p>
</text>
